    pr_ref:  # a71d
    description: "Repro: a repo with pyproject.toml (no dependencies), two modules importing each other, no Cargo.toml -> `hypergumbo survey` prints 'DEPENDENCY-LINKER linker found 3 third-party Rust/Python import edges but 0 TOML dependency declarations'; all 3 edges point at in-repo files. A stdlib-only control repo prints nothing. Fix: skip edges whose dst is a resolved in-repo id (path/`:file` shape) or has dst_ref None; add the first-party case to the WI-juzaj tests. The module docstring was reworded to describe current behaviour in the 2026-10-10 audit PR; revert when fixed.\n\nFound by the 2026-10-10 docstring-staleness audit (reviewer + default-REJECT verifier, reproduced). Notebook: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_10102026.md."  # a71d
    fields:  # a71d
      statement: "The dependency linker's import_edges requirement counts only third-party Rust/Python imports, so a repo with no third-party imports does not warn about missing TOML dependency declarations."  # a71d
      root_cause: "_count_import_edges excludes only Rust toolchain roots and catalogued Python stdlib; a resolved first-party import's dst (python:src/pkg/b.py:1-1:file:file) yields root src/pkg/b and is counted."  # a71d
